# Harness byproducts. `__pycache__` is regenerated on every import and says
# nothing about a run. `evidence/` is the output directory the acceptance
# harness writes when it is given one: each run's harness-run.log, artifact
# identity, store copy, perf log and UI-thread samples.
#
# Acceptance evidence is NOT committed to this repository. A run directory
# records the artifact it drove and the observations it made, and the durable
# conclusions derived from those observations are written up in
# `native/LOCAL-VALIDATION.md` with the hashes that produced them. Committing
# the raw directories instead would put tens of megabytes of per-run logs and
# seeded databases into history, would make every run a diff, and would let a
# stale run directory be read as current evidence -- the exact confusion the
# per-run artifact identity exists to prevent. The record is the report and the
# hashes in it, not the byproduct.
/native/tests/__pycache__/
/native/tests/evidence/

